                <pb facs="0657" n="563" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg563"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Manion to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Johannesburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-13"><hi rendition="#italic">January 13, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Feb. 17.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of your cable of January
                    12, 1896. To this I have cabled reply.</p>
                <p>I have every reason to believe that President Kruger and his Government will take
                    a fair and honorable attitude to all aliens in the Transvaal. I will keep you
                    fully and promptly advised of the progress of all matters affecting American
                    citizens.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. C. Manion</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consular Agent.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
